 * setext headings (a line of text underlined by `=` for depth 1 or `-` for depth 2). Content inside
 * fenced (``` or ~~~) and indented (four spaces) code blocks is ignored. Windows line endings (CRLF)
 * are handled transparently, and all inline formatting is stripped from the returned `value`.
 *
 * @param markdown - The markdown string to parse
 * @returns An array of headings, each with a numeric `depth` (1–6) and a plain-text `value`
 *
 * @example
 * getMarkdownHeadings('# Getting Started\n\nInstallation\n------------')
 * // [
 * //   { depth: 1, value: 'Getting Started' },
 * //   { depth: 2, value: 'Installation' },
 * // ]
